      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19537",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/8b/8bd31a3cf965d67f29b48b6c32e321fcefae4bae5f982fdd1af43e7a1f1fa1b6.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the curve $y = \\frac{1}{x}$ and the $x$-axis from $x = 1$ to $x = 2$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are isosceles right triangles with the hypotenuse lying on the $xy$-plane, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
