      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50445",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ac/ace040efbd40839d6ce12ac27fc51bc477b961bea717f7667ac85630a2046dc3.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the curve $y = \\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis for $-1 \\le x \\le 1$, as shown in the picture. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are equilateral triangles, which of the following gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
